%S A002007 15,200,2672,37600,554880,8514560,134864640,2192440832,36420167680,
%T A002007 616108912640,10585412689920,184315412398080,3246875451260928,
%U A002007 57783302566379520,1037672024481136640,18784958608375152640,342523462671571353600,6286244309981677486080,116050589970458738688000
%N A002007 Number of rooted planar maps with 2n+1 trivalent vertices and a root vertex of valence 5.
%D A002007 R. C. Mullin, E. Nemeth and P. J. Schellenberg, The enumeration of almost cubic maps, pp. 281-295 in Proceedings of the Louisiana Conference on Combinatorics, Graph Theory and Computer Science. Vol. 1, edited R. C. Mullin et al., 1970.
%D A002007 N. J. A. Sloane, A Handbook of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1973 (includes this sequence).
%D A002007 N. J. A. Sloane and Simon Plouffe, The Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1995 (includes this sequence).
%H A002007 Christopher Smolen, <a href="/A002007/b002007.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..200</a>
%H A002007 R. C. Mullin, E. Nemeth and P. J. Schellenberg, <a href="/A002005/a002005.pdf">The enumeration of almost cubic maps</a>, Proc. of the Louisiana Conference on Combinatorics, Graph Theory and Computer Science. Vol. 1, (1970), 291-295 [scanned annotated copy].
%H A002007 Christopher Smolen, <a href="https://github.com/chrispbsmolen/almost-cubic-maps">Almost cubic maps: programs, b-files and three computations of the Mullin-Nemeth-Schellenberg table</a>
%H A002007 Jian Zhou, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.03883">Fat and Thin Emergent Geometries of Hermitian One-Matrix Models</a>, arXiv:1810.03883 [math-ph], 2018.
%F A002007 a(n) = A002005(n+2) - 4*A002005(n+1) - Sum_{i=0..n} A002005(i)*A002005(n-i).
%F A002007 G.f.: (C(x) - 1 - 4*x)/x^2 - 4*(C(x) - 1)/x - C(x)^2, where C(x) is the g.f. of A002005. - _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 07 2026
%o A002007 (Python)
%o A002007 from math import factorial
%o A002007 def dfact(n):
%o A002007     r = 1
%o A002007     while n > 1: r *= n; n -= 2
%o A002007     return r
%o A002007 def c(n): return 2**(2*n+1)*dfact(3*n)//(factorial(n+2)*dfact(n))  # A002005
%o A002007 def d(n): return sum(c(i)*c(n-i) for i in range(n+1))
%o A002007 def a(n): return c(n+2) - 4*c(n+1) - d(n)  # _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 07 2026
%Y A002007 Cf. A002005, A002006, A002008, A002009, A002010.
